settings.definition_quote:
A game is called {\em locally observable} if for every convex set $\cC \subset \RR^d$,
\begin{align}
x - y \in \laspan(A_z : z \in \pP(\cC)) \text{ for all } x, y \in \pP(\cC)\,.  \label{eq:local}
\end{align}

source.quote:
The minimax regret for any finite linear partial monitoring game satisfies
\begin{align*}
R_n^* = 
\begin{cases}
0 & \text{if there is only one Pareto optimal action,} \\
\tilde \Theta(n^{1/2}) & \text{for locally observable games,} \\
\tilde \Theta(n^{2/3}) & \text{for globally observable games,} \\
\Omega(n) & \text{otherwise}\,.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
